# RAVEL's Research Gateway, as a service.
#
# One of three, and the three are the same shape on purpose: gateway,
# supervisor and Temporal worker are all "a process that should always be
# running", and a deployment that had to remember a different rule for each
# would be a deployment whose differences nobody could explain.
#
# ── What an installer changes ─────────────────────────────────────────────
#
# Two things, and they are the two that cannot be guessed: the user the
# service runs as, and where the checkout lives. `scripts/install_services.sh`
# rewrites both from its own arguments and installs the result; this file stays
# concrete rather than templated so that `systemd-analyze verify` can read it
# as the unit it will be. A placeholder would make the file that is checked and
# the file that is installed different files.
#
# ── Restart ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
#
# `Restart=always`, so a crash and an operator's `systemctl stop` are told
# apart by systemd rather than by the service: a stopped unit stays stopped,
# and anything else comes back five seconds later. There is no start limit
# above the defaults, which means a service that cannot start never stays
# down — it comes back, fails, and comes back. That is deliberate: the row
# this process writes carries `started_at`, so a restart loop shows up as a
# start time that keeps moving, which is a better answer than a unit that gave
# up and left an operator to notice.
#
# ── Shutdown ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
#
# `KillSignal=SIGTERM` is the default and is written out because it is load
# bearing here: the application's lifespan records the shutdown when it
# receives one, and that row is what makes a deploy legible as a deploy rather
# than as a death. `TimeoutStopSec` is the window before systemd escalates to
# `SIGKILL` — a kill that skips the lifespan — and it is generous because the
# Gateway may be closing harness runtimes and a database pool.

[Unit]
Description=RAVEL Research Gateway
Documentation=file:///opt/ravel/DEPLOYMENT.md
After=network-online.target docker.service
Wants=network-online.target

[Service]
Type=simple
User=ravel
Group=ravel
WorkingDirectory=/opt/ravel
EnvironmentFile=/opt/ravel/.env
ExecStart=/opt/ravel/.venv/bin/python /opt/ravel/scripts/run_gateway.py
Restart=always
RestartSec=5
KillSignal=SIGTERM
TimeoutStopSec=30
StandardOutput=journal
StandardError=journal
SyslogIdentifier=ravel-gateway

[Install]
WantedBy=multi-user.target
